        "original_id": "ffd0d932-0f2d-560a-99ad-b506ee69b225",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Adventures of Brer Rabbit, Song of the South\n- People: Mark Elliot, Br'er Rabbit\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company\n- Topics: Uncle Remus stories, animated film trailers\n\nFacts:\n- The Adventures of Brer Rabbit is a book, a play, and a film inspired by the Uncle Remus stories.\n- In 1946, The Walt Disney Company adapted Br'er Rabbit for the animated motion picture Song of the South.\n- During the 1980s and 1990s, Mark Elliot was the voice of CBS and FOX.\n- Mark Elliot also voiced theatrical trailers for many non-Disney animated movies, including The Adventures of Brer Rabbit, All Dogs Go to Heaven, Rock-A-Doodle, The Thief and the Cobbler, Once Upon a Forest, The Swan Princess, Balto, and The Prince of Egypt.",
